{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"After having slept through the afternoon; though before that I had seen beautiful gardens, an iron obelisk—70 feet high—erected in memory of the two last Dukes who perished in the war against the French, and in the evening I had seen a bad comedy, we set out again after 10 o’clock on the diligence (though more, according to Wolff’s travesty, on the sloth). The night was beautiful, the stars shone magnificently, — the morning star rose particularly beautifully. Now in the daytime we saw a different physiognomy of nature than before, no longer the barren or fertile plains, — beautiful oak forests, mountains, hills, the gentle slopes covered with fruit fields, the valleys filled with meadows, — in short a homely nature — homely, namely for me, for you yourself, born in half-sand, are in Berlin in the homely element, perhaps in a slightly stronger dose. — So in such a beautiful land we traveled on. With my Englishman, who speaks French, and also some German, I got along very well, he is a young man of 25–26 years, a handsome man, somewhat like the actor Blum, and of such, but better, bearing, good-natured, well-informed, comes from Italy, is going to Paris, to travel from there via Milan to Constantinople, a private person, not too rich — in short as I would also wish for companions in the future. In Nordheim, where we arrived at 3 o’clock in the afternoon (yesterday Wednesday), and the carriage had to wait until about 8 or 9 o’clock in the evening for another, I considered that it would be too uncomfortable for me to spend the third night without a bed and proper sleep; I therefore took extra post — it went first to Göttingen — the scholarly Göttingen; say however only to the dear friend Schulze, that as a proper Berlin professor I did not make much of it, to drive on in 5 minutes, but I did not shake the dust from my feet outside the gate, only because I had not picked any up with them. So I traveled to Münden, where I arrived at 10 o’clock — and slept quietly in bed until 6 o’clock today — and finally here. The road is very charming, Cassel lies very excellently in a wide valley; — the Hercules on Wilhelmshöhe is already visible from several hours away as a peak in the middle of a mountain range. Around Cassel itself it is very beautiful; it has streets — i.e. in one part — in the style of Berlin; the Aue is a layout of approximately the kind of the new garden in Potsdam, beautiful green lawn with healthy varied trees scattered, without any shrubbery, — so transparent everywhere; — it is most charming to walk in it — at the end a beautiful water surface, with hanging willows here and there lining the bank, benches etc., also a house where one can drink coffee in the open air, coffee, i.e. chicory broth; for many days I have only had such, and no coffee to drink, — the whole Brunswick country is covered with fields of this lying root. Tomorrow I will go up to Wilhelmshöhe and into the gallery; today the Englishman has left me in the lurch...."}}],"created":1795218942,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":707,"prompt_tokens":906,"total_tokens":1613,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-HSugsENrUK6C7ITANLrWVj45KeBO0nG2","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":906,"prompt_ms":882.341,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9738863134657837,"prompt_per_second":1026.8138962147286,"predicted_n":707,"predicted_ms":16721.999,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.685550991501415,"predicted_per_second":42.219832688663594}}